Conflicts with core/glibc. In /etc/prt-get.aliases:
    glibc-perf: glibc
This satisfies dependencies only; it does not transfer package ownership.
Do not force conflicts or remove libc first. Keep rescue access and a working
libc archive; binaries using new symbols can prevent rollback.

Appends -O3 to user flags. Unset CC/CXX use gcc/g++ with -march/-mcpu from
flags, or -march=native. Explicit CC/CXX are kept; set both with matching
targets. Packages require compatible CPUs.

Fortify defaults to 3; CFLAGS can set it, and GLIBC_FORTIFY=0/1/2/3 overrides
it. Set _FORTIFY_SOURCE in CFLAGS, not CPPFLAGS. CET defaults to permissive;
GLIBC_CET=no disables it.

Keep the build with pkgmk -kw; run make check as non-root in a writable
work/src/build. The post-install hook reexecutes init and regenerates locales;
use prt-get --install-scripts or runscripts yes. pkgadd does not run it.
